          "package_id": "pkg-ma-s3-trigraph-v2",
          "section_id": "MA-S3",
          "obligation_id": "formula:facet:facet-36188cb856f44d0d",
          "consumer_paragraph_id": "paragraph:MA-S3:6",
          "purpose": "Define the hierarchical graph structure that preserves original text alongside entities.",
          "latex": "\\mathcal{G} = (\\mathcal{V}, \\mathcal{E}, \\mathbf{A}) = (\\mathcal{V}_P \\cup \\mathcal{V}_S \\cup \\mathcal{V}_E, \\mathcal{E}_{contain} \\cup \\mathcal{E}_{mention}, \\mathbf{A}_{contain} \\cup \\mathbf{A}_{mention})",
          "prose_explanation": "This formula defines the static structure of the Tri-Graph. It explicitly separates the node types (passage, sentence, entity) to reflect the hierarchical preservation of text. The adjacency matrices are sparse, reflecting the low density of entity occurrences in large corpora. This structure allows the subsequent retrieval stages to operate on a graph that retains the original textual context (passages/sentences) while enabling entity-based navigation.",
          "markdown_block": "$$\n\\mathcal{G} = (\\mathcal{V}, \\mathcal{E}, \\mathbf{A}) = (\\mathcal{V}_P \\cup \\mathcal{V}_S \\cup \\mathcal{V}_E, \\mathcal{E}_{contain} \\cup \\mathcal{E}_{mention}, \\mathbf{A}_{contain} \\cup \\mathbf{A}_{mention})\n$$",
